## 1. Problem Statement

Recruitment is a critical process for every organization because it helps identify and hire qualified employees. However, many organizations still rely on emails, spreadsheets, or paper documents to manage job vacancies and applications. These manual methods make it difficult to organize applicant information, monitor recruitment progress, schedule interviews, and generate accurate reports. They can also lead to delays, duplicated records, and data management errors.

An Online Job Recruitment and Applicant Tracking System will provide a centralized Oracle database that securely stores recruitment information and automates important recruitment activities. The proposed system will improve efficiency, reduce paperwork, and support better hiring decisions.

---

## 2. Proposed Solution

The proposed solution is an Oracle Database application developed with PL/SQL to manage the complete recruitment process. The system will allow employers to create job vacancies, applicants to submit applications, and administrators to manage recruitment records through a structured relational database.

The system will support employer registration, applicant registration, job posting, application tracking, interview scheduling, and recruitment reporting. Business rules will be implemented using PL/SQL procedures, functions, triggers, packages, cursors, and exception handling to ensure data integrity and process automation.

---

## 3. Data Source

The project will use the **LinkedIn Job Postings Dataset** obtained from Kaggle.

**Dataset:** LinkedIn Job Postings Dataset  
**Source:** Kaggle  
**Link:** https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/arshkon/linkedin-job-postings

This dataset contains real-world recruitment information, including job titles, companies, locations, employment types, industries, skills, and job descriptions. It provides sufficient data for database normalization, Oracle implementation, and reporting.

---

## 4. Planned Database Tables

The proposed database will include the following main tables:

- Users
- Employers
- Applicants
- Jobs
- Applications
- Interviews
- Skills
- Applicant_Skills
- Departments
- Notifications
- Audit_Log

These tables will be related through primary keys and foreign keys to ensure data consistency and support efficient querying.

---

## 5. Planned PL/SQL Features

The project will implement several Oracle PL/SQL features:

- **Procedures** for registering applicants, creating job vacancies, and scheduling interviews.
- **Functions** for counting applicants, checking job availability, and generating recruitment statistics.
- **Triggers** to prevent applications after closing dates and to maintain an audit trail of important changes.
- **Cursors** to retrieve applicant and recruitment information for reports.
- **Packages** to organize recruitment-related procedures and functions.
- **Exception Handling** to manage duplicate applications, invalid records, and other database errors.

---

## 6. Innovation

The planned innovation is an **Oracle APEX web application** connected directly to the Oracle database.

The application will enable employers to post jobs, applicants to submit applications, and administrators to manage recruitment activities through a user-friendly web interface. Oracle APEX will interact with PL/SQL procedures and display real-time information from the database, making the system interactive and easy to use.

